32, 44032], "confidence": 0.85, "narrative": "No time-respecting, 600-unit-gap-bounded path exists from 762 to 1118. 762's out-neighbourhood and 1118's in-neighbourhood are disjoint (no 2-hop route), and the only 3-hop route in the 2-hop subgraph, 762->92->1177->1118, is temporally inverted: 762->92 fires after t=29632 while 1177->1118 fires before t=20032. Node 762 emits nothing before t=20033 and node 1118 receives nothing after t=29632, so influence could only flow backwards in time. High overall volume and both endpoints' healthy degree rule out a mere sparsity artefact.", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**Reasoning trace:**\n\n1. **Static reachability is weak already**: 762's out-neighbours (step_03: 92, 268, 419, 553, 745, 856, 914, 1269, 1346, 1368, 1425, 1466, 1475, 1513, 1532, 1643, 1652) are disjoint from 1118's in-neighbours (step_04: 85, 120, 388, 540, 568, 575, 607, 817, 969, 1107, 1177, 1325, 1399, 1576, 1604, 1633, 1710, 1848). No 2-hop path. The only 3-hop candidate visible in the 2-hop neighbourhood (step_05) is **762 \u2192 92 \u2192 1177 \u2192 1118**.\n\n2. **Temporal ordering kills that path.** Node 762 has **zero** events before t=20033 and is concentrated late (step_06: 0,0,0,2,5,2,4,7 \u2014 bulk in 29633\u201344032). Node 1118 has **zero** events after t=29632 and is concentrated early (step_07: 6,6,4,1,2,0,0,0). Node 1177 is active only 15233\u201334432 (step_08).\n\n3. **Edge-level check.** The 762\u219292 contact exists exactly once over the whole window (step_13) but does *not* occur in [20033, 29632] (step_09) \u2014 so it fires after 29632, i.e. **after** 1118 has already gone silent. Conversely 1177\u21921118 exists exactly once (step_14) but not in [20033, 29632] (step_11), so it fires in 15233\u201320032, **before** 762's first event ever. The 92\u21921177 hop lies in between (step_10) but the chain is ordered backwards.\n\n4. **Confounder control**: both nodes are individually active and well-connected (step_02: 20 and 19 events; step_12), and volume in the window is high (step_01: 4952 events). So the \"absent\" verdict is not from lack of activity \u2014 the two nodes' activity windows are essentially non-overlapping in the required direction, and the 600-unit gap bound cannot bridge the multi-thousand-unit inversion.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_240c5b27\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [762, 1118, 92, 1177],\n  \"window\": [5632, 44032],\n  \"confidence\": 0.85,\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting, 600-unit-gap-bounded path exists from 762 to 1118. 762's out-neighbourhood and 1118's in-neighbourhood are disjoint (no 2-hop route), and the only 3-hop route in the 2-hop subgraph, 762->92->1177->1118, is temporally inverted: 762->92 fires after t=29632 while 1177->1118 fires before t=20032. Node 762 emits nothing before t=20033 and node 1118 receives nothing after t=29632, so influence could only flow backwards in time. High overall volume and both endpoints' healthy degree rule out a mere sparsity artefact.\",\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\":